I had to do some hacking when porting the `Toast` component. The solution is far from perfection as it is using `session$sendCustomMessage` -> `Shiny.addCustomMessageHandler` communication channel, therefore the user is not able to pass the `React` elements (e.g. `ProgressBar`).

@kamilzyla could you please take a look if there is something I am missing about `shiny.react` that could be used to simplify this component? 

Blueprint recommends using the [static method approach](https://blueprintjs.com/docs/#core/components/toast.static-usage), however then you need to instantiate the singleton toaster and refer to it when creating new toast.

